Examples of activities that require permission may include selling the Software, incorporating it into a commercial product or service, or distributing it as part of a paid offering.

## 5. AI-Assisted Modifications Intended for Publication

Any person who intends to publish, distribute, or otherwise make available a modified version of the Software or its source code must not use third-party artificial intelligence systems or AI-powered coding tools to generate, rewrite, or modify any portion of the Software for that purpose without the prior explicit written permission of the copyright holder.

This restriction applies regardless of whether the AI-generated or AI-modified code is subsequently reviewed, edited, or rewritten by a human.

The restriction applies to AI-assisted modifications intended for publication or redistribution, whether the intended publication or redistribution is commercial or non-commercial.

Private modifications that are not intended for publication or redistribution remain permitted under Section 2, subject to the other terms of this license.

For the avoidance of doubt, this section does not prohibit ordinary human modifications intended for non-commercial redistribution, provided all other requirements of this license are met.

